  "pre_gate_answer": "# Briefing\n\n## Likely Questionnaire Identified\nThe evidence suggests the question most likely comes from a **New Jersey-focused private equity due diligence questionnaire**, likely used by a **New Jersey state investment program or pension/investment authority**.\n\n## Basis for This Conclusion\nThe strongest clue is the combination of two specific portfolio-company metrics:\n- **Percentage of current portfolio companies located in New Jersey**\n- **Percentage of current portfolio companies in Life Science/Healthcare**\n\nThis pairing appears designed to assess:\n- **In-state economic exposure**\n- **Sector concentration or specialization**\n\n## What the Evidence Rules Out\nThe cited materials do **not** appear to contain this exact question:\n\n- **ILPA Due Diligence Questionnaire**: broad private equity DDQ, but no visible NJ/Life Science question\n- **INREV Due Diligence Questionnaire**: focused on non-listed real estate, not relevant\n- **OCERS Investment Consultant Services RFP**: consultant selection document, not a GP portfolio exposure DDQ\n- **Calamos/Aksia Private Markets DDQ**: general manager-evaluation questionnaire, but no visible exact match\n\n## Confidence and Limitation\nThe identification is **probable, not definitive**.  \nThe excerpts do **not** show the exact questionnaire title or the exact line containing the question.\n\n## Bottom Line\nThe most likely source is a **New Jersey private equity due diligence questionnaire**, rather than ILPA, INREV, OCERS, or the Calamos/Aksia private markets DDQ.",
